  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "When Blood Sea Ancestor caused chaos in the five regions, a Heavenly Court predecessor followed Fate Gu’s revelation, found a wild rank eight blood relation Immortal Gu, captured it, and added it to the house so every blood path cultivator below rank nine could be detected. Heavenly Court used that information to suppress blood path in Central Continent and passed news to the other four regions. Red Heart Traveler, the then Board Lord and a sole blood path cultivator, cultivates inside the house for years, then leaves and names Fang Zheng the next Demon Judgment Board Lord, with past Board Lords’ inheritance and cultivation experiences inside the board.",
      "chapters": [
        1886
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_blood_sea_ancestor",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "gu_fate_gu",
        "gu_blood_relation_gu",
        "reg_central_continent",
        "char_red_heart_traveler",
        "char_fang_zheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page is filed under gu-houses because Demon Judgment Board is a named Immortal Gu House. It is Heavenly Court equipment, not a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu_house"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fairy Zi Wei sends Qin Ding Ling to reinforce Duke Long with Gu Yue Fang Zheng, who has been cultivating in Demon Judgment Board. The house appears as a red tombstone with countless moving words, named the rank eight Immortal Gu House Demon Judgment Board. Fang Yuan guesses Fang Zheng is inside; Fang Zheng and Qin Ding Ling both ride in the board. After becoming Board Lord, Fang Zheng uses past Board Lords’ experience to create the killer move blood-kin heart revenge.",
      "chapters": [
        1939
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "tombstone-form",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fairy_zi_wei",
        "char_qin_ding_ling",
        "char_duke_long",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan tries to destroy Demon Judgment Board and kill Fang Zheng, but Duke Long and Cang Xuan Zi interfere, and landed hits only shake and crack the house before the Gu Immortals inside fully repair it. Demon Judgment Board differs from most of Heavenly Court’s Immortal Gu Houses: it is comprehensive in defense, movement, recovery, and other roles, with no clear weaknesses.",
      "chapters": [
        1940
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "comprehensive-roles",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_cang_xuan_zi",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Zheng is the current owner of Demon Judgment Board; even at rank seven cultivation, with this board he can fight most rank eight Gu Immortals.",
      "chapters": [
        1986
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "board-lord-strength",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Three Gu Immortals ride inside rank eight Immortal Gu House Demon Judgment Board in immemorial black heaven. Activated, it becomes a blood colored meteor that pierces a grotto-heaven wall into Great Wisdom grotto-heaven. It showed solid performance in the fate war, survived that war, and is one of the top rank eight Immortal Gu Houses in the world.",
      "chapters": [
        1989
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fate-war-performance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_great_wisdom_grotto_heaven"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In Crazed Demon Cave, Fang Yuan’s killer move lands on Demon Judgment Board and sweeps it deep into dense fog toward the five regional walls, while he plans to destroy the board after allies stall Divine Emperor City. Inside the board, Fairy Ming Hao and Gu Yue Fang Zheng charge a formation; dense five colored smoke dims the board, Fang Zheng suffers backlash, and a full powered blood red beam fails to remove even one layer of the five regional limit formation’s defense. Fairy Ming Hao later stores the Immortal Gu House in her aperture; neither side destroys the other’s prize in that exchange.",
      "chapters": [
        2174
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "regional-walls-clash",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_crazed_demon_cave",
        "house_divine_emperor_city",
        "char_fairy_ming_hao"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At Book Mountain the board appears again as a huge red tombstone with moving text and dense blood path aura. Under Fang Zheng it crashes into Unbreakable Golden Fortress, fires a blood red beam, and forces the fortress down from mid-mountain; Demon Judgment Board is a peak creation far beyond that rank eight fortress. Past Board Lords’ wills help Fang Zheng repair the house during the fight.",
      "chapters": [
        2179
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "book-mountain-clash",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_book_mountain",
        "house_unbreakable_golden_fortress"
      ]
    }
  ],
